# Timestamped .env copies. The stock rule matches ".env.backup" exactly, so a
# dated one — which is what any real backup looks like — slipped past it
# carrying APP_KEY and the IP hash salt.
.env.backup-*
.env.*.bak

# Scratch output from one-off scripts in tools/. The scripts themselves are
# kept; what they print is not.
/tools/_*

# The raw brand identity kit.
#
# Kept out of the repository on purpose, and this is not tidiness. It holds
# licensed font files (.otf) and the brand guideline in Illustrator source —
# and §10.3 already records that web-embedding rights for the display face are
# unverified. Pushing those to a public repository would redistribute
# someone's licensed font and publish Amad Craft's confidential design source,
# and git history makes both effectively permanent.
#
# The site does not need them to run: the subset woff2 files it actually
# serves live in public/fonts and are committed. If the kit should travel with
# the code, make the repository private first and remove this rule.
/هوية امد الحرف/

# Backups are data, never code.
storage/backups/
